+//! Playground live editing (`playground_live`): the shared document is the session's presentations, `{documents: [{id,
+//! name, ...presentation}]}`: the one active when the session started (or that a joiner's active window takes) and each
+//! one opened, created or imported since by anyone, which opens behind the others' own. Each is its model as JSON
+//! (written as the native save writes it, non-finite numbers as 0) with its media's bytes and without the id counter, the
+//! drawing guides or this person's views (selection, current slide, zoom, panes). Closing one is personal: the session
+//! goes on with it, and File › Home lists the session's presentations to go to or open again. Native undo history stays
+//! local; while connected, Undo and Redo of the session's presentations go to the session.
+//!
+//! Presence: the presentation and slide each person shows, their pointer on it (slide points), their selected shapes and
+//! what they are doing before it reaches the document (shapes moved, resized or rotated, a shape or text box being drawn,
+//! ink or a freeform path), drawn over the others' slides in their color and eased toward where they are; each slide's
+//! thumbnail (the Slides pane, the Slide Sorter) shows a badge with the initial of each other person on it. Typing needs
+//! nothing of its own: each keystroke edits the document (between keystrokes the app is quiet), so it reaches the others
+//! at once.
+//!
+//! Upstream calls in through hooks (rules in patches/powerpoint.yaml): `deckcraft_engine::LIVE_UNDO` at the top of
+//! `Session::execute`, `deckcraft_model::LIVE_ALLOC` at the top of `Presentation::alloc_id`, `deckcraft_ui_egui::LIVE_PAINT`
+//! at the top of the canvas's overlays, `deckcraft_ui_egui::LIVE_THUMB` on each slide thumbnail and
+//! `deckcraft_ui_egui::LIVE_HOME` at the top of File › Home.
+
+// The frame hook and drawing run in the browser only.
+#![cfg_attr(test, allow(dead_code))]
+
